BREAKING NEWS: 
Dalrada Financial Corporation Completes Acquisition of M&M 
Nursing; Nurse Staffing Company Expected to Contribute 
Over $3 Million in Revenues 

SAN DIEGO, July 20 /PRNewswire-FirstCall/ -- Dalrada Financial Corporation 
(OTC Bulletin Board: DRDF 
- News) today announced 
that has completed its acquisition of M&M Nursing Services. The acquisition was 
accomplished through the payment of cash and Dalrada securities.  While the 
finalization of the acquisition is pursuant to an Asset Purchase Agreement dated 
June 28, 2004, M&M Nursing operations have been operating as part of Dalrada's 
Jackson Staffing subsidiary since early May. M&M Nursing Services, founded in 
1995, is headquartered in Southfield, Michigan, with additional offices in San 
Antonio and Dallas, Texas. The Company provides nursing professionals to 
hospitals and other health care facilities on a temporary basis. The company 
currently serves all the major hospitals throughout the Detroit metropolitan 
area and has a very strong reputation in its industry.  Management 
estimates that the addition of M&M Nursing will add approximately $400 thousand 
in fourth-quarter revenues, which will be reported on Dalrada's annual report on 
Form 10-KSB for the year-ended June 30, 2004. On an annualized basis, management 
estimates the revenue contribution from M&M Nursing to be $3 million.



